1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:00,850
Last video.

2
00:00:00,855 --> 00:00:04,699
Where to look when something isn't
behaving, and the four problems that

3
00:00:04,759 --> 00:00:06,568
account for most questions we get.

4
00:00:07,778 --> 00:00:11,831
The app ships its own documentation — no
tab-switching to a website.

5
00:00:11,891 --> 00:00:16,730
Open Documentation from the nav and you
get eight cards covering the quick start,

6
00:00:16,790 --> 00:00:21,629
model files, every settings group, preview
behaviour, block placement, embedding,

7
00:00:21,689 --> 00:00:23,564
plan limits and troubleshooting.

8
00:00:24,424 --> 00:00:28,475
The quick start card is the four-step
version of this whole series, so it's the

9
00:00:28,535 --> 00:00:31,389
one to send a colleague who just needs to
add one model.

10
00:00:32,249 --> 00:00:37,531
Model files spells out the rules in one
place: glb recommended, gltf accepted,

11
00:00:37,591 --> 00:00:43,217
twenty megabyte ceiling but aim under ten
for page speed, and the reminder that iOS

12
00:00:43,277 --> 00:00:44,929
AR needs a separate USDZ.

13
00:00:45,789 --> 00:00:48,515
Problem one: the block renders nothing at
all.

14
00:00:48,575 --> 00:00:52,088
Almost always this means the product has
no model assigned.

15
00:00:52,148 --> 00:00:57,054
The block outputs nothing rather than an
empty box, which is correct but does look

16
00:00:57,114 --> 00:00:57,720
like a bug.

17
00:00:57,780 --> 00:01:02,686
Assign a model, or paste a manual glb URL
into the block to prove the block itself

18
00:01:02,746 --> 00:01:03,346
works.

19
00:01:03,909 --> 00:01:08,178
Problem two: you save, but the storefront
keeps showing the old settings.

20
00:01:08,238 --> 00:01:10,846
Go to Setup and check storefront read
access.

21
00:01:10,906 --> 00:01:15,589
Without it your theme genuinely cannot
read the config, no matter how many times

22
00:01:15,649 --> 00:01:16,249
you save.

23
00:01:16,183 --> 00:01:18,139
Run the button, then hard-refresh.

24
00:01:18,999 --> 00:01:22,211
That's this column, right here. Every row
should read Ready.

25
00:01:22,821 --> 00:01:26,147
Problem three: a page block says the Model
ID isn't found.

26
00:01:26,207 --> 00:01:31,051
That ID is resolved through the shop
library metafield, and Setup is what

27
00:01:31,111 --> 00:01:35,779
Run Setup, then compare your ID against
the list in What the theme block can see.

28
00:01:35,839 --> 00:01:38,990
If it isn't there, copy it again from the
model's page.

29
00:01:39,850 --> 00:01:41,814
Problem four: the model goes white.

30
00:01:41,874 --> 00:01:46,034
That usually means the viewer is
re-initialising because you just changed

31
00:01:46,094 --> 00:01:49,677
something structural, like tone mapping or
the environment map.

32
00:01:49,737 --> 00:01:51,990
Wait a second, or revert that one field.

33
00:01:52,850 --> 00:01:56,895
And one more that catches people: if
Preview or Save And View seems to do

34
00:01:56,955 --> 00:01:59,201
nothing, your browser blocked the pop-up.

35
00:01:59,261 --> 00:02:03,700
Both need to be a direct click, so don't
trigger them from a keyboard macro or a

36
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:04,360
script.

37
00:02:04,953 --> 00:02:09,020
All four of those are written up in the
Troubleshooting card at the bottom of the

38
00:02:09,080 --> 00:02:12,129
documentation page, so you don't have to
remember this video.

39
00:02:12,989 --> 00:02:17,013
Back on the dashboard, Help and resources
is the fastest route out.

40
00:02:17,073 --> 00:02:22,012
The video tutorial, the documentation, a
link to leave a review, and Get support —

41
00:02:22,072 --> 00:02:23,962
which reaches our team directly.

42
00:02:24,822 --> 00:02:29,755
If you do write in, three things make it
fast: your store domain and the product or

43
00:02:29,815 --> 00:02:34,508
Model ID involved, a screenshot of your
Setup page, and the exact error text if

44
00:02:34,568 --> 00:02:35,290
one appeared.

45
00:02:35,350 --> 00:02:38,599
The Setup screenshot answers most
questions on its own.

46
00:02:39,459 --> 00:02:40,897
And that's the whole app.

47
00:02:40,957 --> 00:02:45,874
Setup once, assign a model, add the block
once, then tune the viewer as much as you

48
00:02:45,934 --> 00:02:46,534
like.

49
00:02:46,234 --> 00:02:50,970
Thanks for watching — and if the app is
working well for you, a review genuinely

50
00:02:51,030 --> 00:02:51,630
helps.
